+**The page's settings, checked in a real page (2026-11-07, G4):** `node tools/preview/power-page-check.mjs --dir <the build's web folder>` opens the built page through the guarded launcher with the black box on (one browser at a time, below-normal, with a time limit), clicks through the How to play card and the flashing notice as the smoke check does, lets the match start, and reads the black box's own record of the match's setup together with the two sliders, for six addresses: no word, `?power=1`, `?power=0`, `?power=off`, `?travel=1.5&flatout=6000` and an out-of-range pair. Expected: power true with `travel` 2 and `flatOut` 5000 and two sliders; power false with neither key and no slider; the two words reach the setup; a slider moved sets `window.__travel` / `window.__flatout` and is remembered (`orb_travel`, `orb_flatout`) with the labels "how far a launch carries x1.55" and "flat-out flight base speed 6200". `?flatout=N` (3,500 to 7,000) now starts the slider at N like `?travel=`: before, the page head set the slider's value first and the game took it first, so the word never reached the setup on the web (found by this check). An out-of-range word is ignored by the head.
diff --git a/tools/preview/power-page-check.mjs b/tools/preview/power-page-check.mjs
